    "title": "New flights to Myrtle Beach and expanded terminal debut at Raleigh Co. airport - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Caleb Okes ,\n3 hours ago\nBEAVER, WV (WVNS) – It was a big moment for Raleigh County Memorial Airport.\nGHSP encourages drivers to “Secure Your Load” before hitting the road Not only did the airport’s leadership team celebrate their completed terminal expansion project, but they also kicked off a brand new seasonal flight special with Contour Airlines.\nFolks can now catch flights to Myrtle Beach and back right from RCMA for less than $70 one way. Airport manager Robert Runion told 59News this new seasonal flight is great for vacationers who want to save the stops at gas stations with how high prices are right now.\n“A commercial air carrier brings that funding to you and if you get a certain amount of boardings, you get additional. So, really invest in the airport which also invests back to the community,” said Runion.\nThese seasonal flights will take place on Wednesdays and Saturdays through August 2026.\nFor their expanded terminal, they were able to increase their screen room capacity and add a pilots lounge among other things. This was a 1600 square foot project.\nRunion thanked the many groups who partnered with them to make all these different things come together.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WVNS.\n2",
    "summary": "BEAVER, WV (WVNS) – It was a big moment for Raleigh County Memorial Airport. GHSP encourages drivers to “Secure Your Load” before hitting the road Not only did the airport’s leadership team celebrate their completed terminal expansion project, but they also kicked off a brand new seasonal flight special with Contour Airlines. Airport manager Robert Runion told 59News this new seasonal flight is great for vacationers who want to save the stops at gas stations with how high prices are right now.",
